{extends "modules/daily-ledger/layouts/app.disyl"}

{block content}
<div class="flex items-center justify-between mb-6"><div><h2 class="text-lg font-semibold text-gray-900">Production Forecast</h2><p class="text-sm text-gray-500">Read-only suggestions, one row per BRANCH, product and shift, from recorded official sales, that branch's own variances and its own counted stock on hand.</p></div><span class="rounded bg-indigo-50 px-3 py-1 text-sm text-indigo-700">Target: {target_date}</span></div>
<div class="rounded-lg bg-amber-50 p-4 text-sm text-amber-800 mb-6 ring-1 ring-inset ring-amber-200">Forecasts are suggestions only. This page never creates or changes production or ledger entries.</div>
<div class="rounded-lg bg-slate-50 p-4 text-sm text-slate-700 mb-4 ring-1 ring-inset ring-slate-200">
    <strong>One row per branch &mdash; each branch's suggestion is its own.</strong> Sales, variance and stock on hand
    are read for that branch alone, so branch A needing 100 and branch B needing 10 no longer average into a single figure
    nobody can action. <em>Stock applied</em> is that branch's own latest counted ending: a supplying branch is never credited
    with the commissary's undelivered finished goods, which no branch has received and which would otherwise offset
    every branch that commissary supplies. Each row states whether that branch produces its own goods or is supplied.
    <span class="mt-1 block"><strong>Every product that moved in the window is listed</strong>, including one that sold nothing.
    A row with <em>0 days</em> carries movement but no measured sales, so its 0 suggestion means "no sales were recorded",
    not "demand was measured as zero" &mdash; it is labelled as such rather than quietly dropped.</span>
    <span class="mt-1 block"><strong>The average is per day the product could actually be BOUGHT, not per day the branch traded.</strong>
    Three different things are kept apart, because collapsing them is how a forecast understates demand:
    a day the product was <em>sold</em>; a day it was <em>on the shelf and sold nothing</em> (a measured zero, which counts);
    and a day it <em>could not be bought</em> or nobody recorded it (which counts as nothing at all).
    Measured over 2026-09-28..2026-10-11: 1,578 of 2,215 zero-sale days &mdash; 71% &mdash; were days the product was not stocked,
    and they were dragging the averages down; one stream read 0.73/day that way while selling 8 units on its one buyable day.</span>
    <span class="mt-1 block"><strong>Stock on hand is dated.</strong> Each row shows the as-of date of the count it applied and
    flags a count older than the window, so a stale shelf is never read as current stock.</span>
</div>
<div class="rounded-lg bg-indigo-50 p-4 text-sm text-indigo-900 mb-4 ring-1 ring-inset ring-indigo-200">
    <strong>How the target is calculated.</strong> Target production = expected sales &divide; (1 &minus; spoilage rate), using each product's own spoilage rate (its wastage &divide; produced from the production ledger - the same rate the Production Efficiency view reports). A product spoiling 20% is produced at expected sales &divide; 0.8, so a product that spoils worse than a flat margin is never under-produced.
    <span class="mt-1 block">{spoilage_products_with_rate} product(s) carry a measurable spoilage rate; {spoilage_products_without_rate} product(s) have no spoilage history in this window and are shown as <em>not measurable</em>, with a target that is the expected sales and no gross-up - never an assumed rate.</span>
</div>
<form class="card mb-6" action="{base_url}/admin/forecast" method="GET" onsubmit="return window.dlLoadForm(this)"><div class="card-body grid grid-cols-1 sm:grid-cols-2 lg:grid-cols-5 gap-3 items-end">
<div class="form-group">{include "modules/daily-ledger/admin/partials/scope-filter.disyl"}</div><div class="form-group"><label class="form-label">Target date</label><input class="form-input" type="date" name="target_date" value="{target_date}"></div>
<div class="form-group"><label class="form-label">History window</label><input class="form-input" type="number" min="3" max="90" name="window" value="{window}"></div>
<div class="form-group"><label class="form-label">Branch</label><select class="form-input" name="branch_id"><option value="">All</option>{foreach branches as branch}<option value="{branch.id}" {if branch.id == filters.branch_id}selected{/if}>{branch.name}</option>{/foreach}</select></div>
<div class="form-group"><label class="form-label">Product</label><select class="form-input" name="product_id"><option value="">All</option>{foreach products as product}<option value="{product.id}" {if product.id == filters.product_id}selected{/if}>{product.name}</option>{/foreach}</select></div>
<div class="form-group"><label class="flex items-center gap-2 text-sm text-gray-700"><input type="hidden" name="empty_rows" value="include"><input type="checkbox" name="empty_rows" value="exclude" {if exclude_empty}checked{/if}><span>Hide products with no movement or sales</span></label><span class="text-xs text-muted">Excludes rows where nothing sold and nothing moved. Measured over the last window: those are the majority of rows, and none of them is a production target.</span></div>
<div class="form-group"><label class="form-label">Sort by suggested qty</label><select class="form-input" name="sort_dir"><option value="desc" {if sort_dir == 'desc'}selected{/if}>Highest first</option><option value="asc" {if sort_dir == 'asc'}selected{/if}>Lowest first</option></select></div>
<button class="btn btn-primary" type="submit">Apply filters</button></div></form>
<div class="card"><div class="card-header"><span>Suggested Production</span><span class="text-sm text-muted">{forecast_total} total branch product shift(s) &middot; {forecast_page_count} on this page &middot; {product_count} product(s)</span></div><div class="px-4 py-3 text-sm text-gray-700 border-b border-gray-200">Showing {showing_from}&ndash;{showing_to} of {forecast_total} results.</div><div class="table-wrap"><table><thead><tr><th>Branch</th><th>Product</th><th>Shift</th><th>Days</th><th>Avg Sales</th><th>Variance Adj.</th><th>Expected Sales</th><th>Spoilage Rate</th><th>Spoilage Gross-up</th><th>Target</th><th>Stock Applied</th><th>Suggested</th></tr></thead><tbody>
{if rows | count == 0}<tr><td colspan="12" class="text-center text-muted">No finalized sales history for the selected scope.</td></tr>{/if}
{foreach rows as row}<tr><td><strong>{row.branch_name}</strong><div class="text-xs text-muted">{row.source_label}</div></td><td><strong>{row.product_name}</strong><div class="text-xs text-muted">{row.sku}</div></td><td>{row.shift}</td><td>{if row.sample_days > 0}{row.sample_days}{/if}{if row.sample_days == 0}<span class="text-amber-700" title="{row.sales_basis}">0 &mdash; not buyable</span>{/if}{if row.censored_days > 0} <span class="text-amber-700" title="{row.censored_days} day(s) in this window the product could not be bought at all (nothing in stock and nothing received). Those days are EXCLUDED from the average: a day the product was unbuyable is not evidence of low demand.">+{row.censored_days} unbuyable</span>{/if}{if row.unknown_days > 0} <span class="text-muted" title="{row.unknown_days} day(s) the branch recorded this shift with NO row for this product. Absence of a row is not a recorded zero, so those days are EXCLUDED rather than counted as zero demand.">+{row.unknown_days} unknown</span>{/if}{if row.evidence_status == 'insufficient'} <span class="text-red-700" title="Fewer than 5 buyable days: this average is too thin to plan production on. Treat it as a starting point to confirm, not a target.">low evidence</span>{/if}{if row.evidence_status == 'provisional'} <span class="text-amber-700" title="5 to 9 buyable days: workable but thin. More counted days will steady it.">provisional</span>{/if}</td><td>{row.average_sales}</td><td>{row.variance_adjustment}</td><td>{row.expected_sales}</td><td>{if row.spoilage_available}{row.spoilage_rate | number_format:2}%{/if}{if row.spoilage_available == false}<span class="text-amber-700" title="no measurable wastage/produced history for this product in the window">not measurable</span>{/if}</td><td>{row.spoilage_gross_up}</td><td>{row.target_production}</td><td>{row.inventory_applied}{if row.stock_state != ''} <span class="text-amber-700" title="{row.stock_state}">stale</span>{/if}{if row.stock_as_of != ''} <span class="text-xs text-muted" title="stock on hand as of {row.stock_as_of}">as of {row.stock_as_of}</span>{/if}</td><td class="font-semibold text-indigo-700">{row.suggested_production}</td></tr>{/foreach}
</tbody></table></div>{if pager_links | count > 0}<nav class="flex flex-wrap items-center gap-2 border-t border-gray-200 px-4 py-3" aria-label="Forecast result pages"><span class="mr-1 text-sm text-muted">Page {page} of {total_pages}</span>{foreach pager_links as pager_link}<a href="{pager_link.url | raw}" class="inline-flex min-w-8 items-center justify-center rounded border px-3 py-1 text-sm {if pager_link.current}border-indigo-600 bg-indigo-600 text-white{else}border-gray-300 bg-white text-gray-700 hover:bg-gray-50{/if}" {if pager_link.current}aria-current="page"{/if}>{pager_link.label}</a>{/foreach}</nav>{/if}</div>
{/block}
